:: ===========================================================================
:: pie.sca — Proto-Indo-European -> Solar Speech (Sauleis Bazdā) for SCArs.
::
:: This encodes stage 0a-9 of the Ligurian grammar's §II sound-change table
:: (lib/site/ligurian-grammar.md), so the /derive page can derive Solar Speech
:: from PIE roots in real time — and chain into ligurian.sca (Solar -> Heart).
::
:: Notation: rule parts are SPACE-SEPARATED graphemes; `FROM > TO / PRE _ POST`;
:: `#` is a word boundary; classes expand host-side. Multi-character graphemes
:: (h₂, ǵʰ, kʷ, m̥, ā …) are ordinary tokens — the segmenter longest-matches.
:: Apply with:   latte sca --file lib/pie.sca dʰeh₁s mr̥to ǵʰel gʷih₃w nokʷt
:: ===========================================================================

class V = a e i o u ā ē ī ō ū
class C = p t k b d g s z m n r l w y bʰ dʰ gʰ ǵʰ ǵ ḱ kʷ gʷ gʷʰ

:: --- stage 0: strip PIE accent marks ---------------------------------------
é > e
á > a
í > i
ó > o
ú > u
ḗ > ē
ṓ > ō

:: --- 0a: laryngeal coloring -------------------------------------------------
h₂ e > a
h₃ e > o
h₁ e > e
e h₂ > ā
e h₃ > ō
e h₁ > ē
o h₂ > ā
o h₃ > ō

:: --- 0b: laryngeal lengthening of i/u ---------------------------------------
i h₁ > ī
i h₂ > ī
i h₃ > ī
u h₁ > ū
u h₂ > ū
u h₃ > ū

:: --- 0c: word-initial laryngeal before a consonant --------------------------
h₂ > a / # _ C
h₃ > o / # _ C

:: --- 0d: interconsonantal h₂ -> ā; remaining laryngeals lost ----------------
h₂ > ā / C _ C
h₁ >
h₂ >
h₃ >

:: --- 1: syllabic resonants ---------------------------------------------------
m̥ > a m
n̥ > a n
r̥ > a r
l̥ > a l

:: --- 2a: depalatalization before a nasal -------------------------------------
ḱ > k / _ m
ḱ > k / _ n

:: --- 2b: satemization (the dominant reflex) ----------------------------------
ḱ > s
ǵʰ > z
ǵ > z

:: --- 3: labiovelar split ------------------------------------------------------
kʷ > k
gʷʰ > b / _ ī
gʷʰ > g
gʷ > b / _ ī
gʷ > g

:: --- 4: deaspiration (the rbʰ cluster devoices) -------------------------------
r bʰ > r p
bʰ > b
dʰ > d
gʰ > g

:: --- 5a: vocalism: o -> a in a non-initial closed syllable --------------------
o > a / C _ C C
o > a / V _ C C

:: --- 5b: long-vowel shortening before w ---------------------------------------
ā > a / _ w

:: --- 5c: diphthong normalization ----------------------------------------------
e y > e i
o y > o i
o w > o u
a w > a u

:: --- 6: cluster changes --------------------------------------------------------
s r > s t r
w r > b r
d t > s t
t t > s t
l n > l l
d w > d
d y > z
t y > s

:: --- 7: intervocalic s-voicing --------------------------------------------------
s > z / V _ V

:: --- 8: semivowel hardening after a sibilant (V[s,z]_) ---------------------------
w > b / V s _
w > b / V z _

:: --- 9: late syncope --------------------------------------------------------------
u e l > u l
